From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:26:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10806/11171] Record the precondition my own falsification test
 was missing

The .605 test I filed an hour ago -- document rewritten with a matching contract
closes the regression, skipped again means my instruction was not the cause -- is
invalid unless the conductor is restarted first.

The corrected instruction is committed but not loaded. The conductor is a long-lived
--loop process started at 15:06Z and reads research_conductor.py only at startup; the
both-files-required fix landed at 21:15Z. If .605 plans on the current process and
skips the document, that shows the old instruction is still in memory, not that my
change was innocent.

The failure mode is silent and self-flattering, which is why it is written down:
forget the restart, watch .605 skip the document, and clear my own change on the
strength of a test that never ran it.

A restart was deferred at 21:30Z because a codex child was 41 minutes into a task and
a restart kills the in-flight child. Milestone .605 cannot plan until .604's seven
tasks finish, so there is room; the restart must land in a gap between tasks and
before .605 plans.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
